<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Inkwell — Compose</title>

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;600;700&family=Newsreader:opsz,wght@6..72,400;6..72,500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="shell shell--narrow">
      <!-- ========== top bar ========== -->
      <header class="topbar">
        <a class="brand" href="/">
          <span class="brand__mark">✒</span>
          <span class="brand__name">Inkwell</span>
        </a>

        <nav class="nav">
          <a class="nav__link" href="/">Home</a>
          <a class="nav__link" href="/blogs">Blogs</a>
          <a class="nav__link nav__link--active" href="/compose">Compose</a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <!-- ========== page heading ========== -->
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="hero__kicker">Nothing saves until you publish</p>

        <h1 class="hero__title">
          New
          <span>post</span>
        </h1>
      </section>

      <!--
        TODO (student) — error banner

        Show this banner ONLY when your route passes an `error` message
        (for example when the title is too short, or a field is blank).
        Wrap it in an if, and print the message where the sample text is.

        Because it only appears when something went wrong, it is a
        rarely-seen element — that is why it gets its own little entrance
        animation in the stylesheet.
      -->
      <div class="flash">
        <span>⚠</span>
        <span>Sample error message goes here</span>
      </div>

      <!--
        TODO (student) — wire up the form

        1. Point `action` at the route that saves a post, and set `method`
           to the verb used for creating data.
        2. Leave the `name` attributes exactly as they are — your route will
           read req.body.title, req.body.author and req.body.content.
        3. Bonus: if the submit fails and you re-render this page, pass the
           values back and print them into the `value` attribute (title,
           author) and between the <textarea> tags (content) so the writer
           does not lose their work.
      -->
      <form class="composer" action="TODO" method="TODO">
        <div class="field-group">
          <label class="label" for="title">Title</label>
          <input
            class="field"
            type="text"
            id="title"
            name="title"
            placeholder="Something worth clicking on"
            minlength="3"
            maxlength="120"
            required
            autocomplete="off"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="field-group">
          <label class="label" for="author">Author</label>
          <input
            class="field"
            type="text"
            id="author"
            name="author"
            placeholder="Your name"
            minlength="2"
            maxlength="60"
            required
            autocomplete="off"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="field-group">
          <label class="label" for="content">Post</label>
          <textarea
            class="field field--area"
            id="content"
            name="content"
            placeholder="Start typing. Line breaks are kept exactly as you type them."
            minlength="10"
            required
          ></textarea>
          <p class="hint">Minimum 10 characters. Plain text only.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="composer__actions">
          <button class="btn" type="submit">Publish</button>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/blogs">Cancel</a>
        </div>
      </form>

      <p class="footnote">Built with Express · EJS · MongoDB</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
